    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 23 tests run, 0 failures/errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`), where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter.\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name.\n3. **Schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `membership_number` column.\n4. **`AssignMembershipNumber.java`** \u2014 new OfficeFloor function that reads the owner via `@Val`, computes `customerCode + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`, and sets it.\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignMembership` step in after `assignNamesakeCount` (so `customerCode` and `registrationDate` are already set) and before `save`, under the transaction governance.\n\nThe value is derived purely from the owner's own fields, matching the seed-independent Cp14 test.",
